{
  "_README": [
    "Adi's 2026 ranks. This file wins over anything the model generates.",
    "",
    "HOW TO USE:",
    "  1. Put names in the order you want, top first.",
    "  2. Run: node scripts/build-rankings.js",
    "  3. git add -A && git commit -m \"my 2026 ranks\" && git push",
    "",
    "RULES:",
    "  - A tab left as [] uses the generated order. 'overall' is empty, so it stays VORP-generated.",
    "  - Names match against data/projections-2026.json to pull team and projected PPG.",
    "    Spelling must match, case doesn't.",
    "  - A player with no projection still ranks; the row just shows no PPG rather than",
    "    an invented one. The build prints those names so you can see them.",
    "  - Use {\"name\": \"X\", \"team\": \"BUF\", \"pos\": \"WR\"} for players with no projection,",
    "    so the team and badge still render.",
    "  - Invalid JSON aborts the build instead of publishing a half-right board.",
    "    A trailing comma after the last item is the usual culprit."
  ],
